  "body": "As noted in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/7348#discussion_r754037053, we sometimes say something vague like \"the WindowProxy that corresponds to _window_\", and sometimes we do something rigorous-but-hard-to-understand, like \"_window_'s relevant Realm.[[GlobalEnv]].[[GlobalThisValue]]\" or \"_window_'s relevant Realm.[[GlobalEnv]]'s EnvironmentRecord's [[GlobalThisValue]]\".\r\n\r\nWe should create a wrapper definition, e.g. \"_window_'s corresponding WindowProxy\", and use that throughout.",
